      "message": "Reusing git cl\u0027s patchset logic is what I asked for, but the CLI wrapper adds problems the helpers don\u0027t have:\n\n- `CMDtry_results` builds `Changelist(issue\u003d...)` with no host or project, so they come from the cwd\u0027s git remote. `--host` and `crrev.com/i/...` are parsed and then dropped, and a chromium/src CL queried from a depot_tools checkout 404s.\n- `try-results` exits early in Cog (`IsEnvCog()`).\n- `--json -` shares stdout with the `bb auth-login` warning, which breaks `json.loads()`.\n\nCould you call the helpers in-process instead? `Changelist` already accepts both:\n\n```\ncl \u003d git_cl.Changelist(issue\u003dcl_number, codereview_host\u003dhost, gerrit_project\u003dproject)\npatchset \u003d patchset or cl.GetMostRecentCqPatchset()\nbuilds \u003d git_cl._fetch_tryjobs(cl, \u0027cr-buildbucket.appspot.com\u0027, patchset)\n```\n\nThat keeps `--host` and the URL host meaningful, and there\u0027s no JSON to parse. The project can come from the URL; for a bare number, the cwd default is fine.",
