      "side": 1,
      "message": "`git cl issue` prints `Issue number: \u003cid\u003e (\u003curl\u003e)`, and the URL carries the host. Keeping only the digits means auto-detect on a chrome-internal-review branch (e.g. under `clank/`) or on Dawn/ANGLE etc. silently queries chromium-review instead.\n\nSince `parse_cl_arg()` already handles `https://\u003chost\u003e/\u003ccl\u003e`, returning the URL when present fixes it:\n\n```\nmatch \u003d re.search(\n    r\"Issue number:\\s*(\\d+)(?:\\s*\\((https?://[^\\s)]+)\\))?\", output\n)\nif match:\n    return match.group(2) or match.group(1)\n```\n\nPlease add an internal-host case to `test_get_current_branch_cl`.",
